; Period commentary for 2023. Each entry is a transaction with no postings,
; dated at the end of the period it covers, so it never affects balances.
; Read with e.g. `hledger print tag:commentary -p 2023q1`. Note that any
; `word:` in the text below would be parsed as a tag, so avoid writing that.

2023-02-28 February 2023  ; commentary:
    ; I moved hosting of mineshspc.com under Nevarro LLC late in the month,
    ; hence the low server costs. I was spinning servers up and down to find
    ; the right setup, which is why there were 3 servers/IPs on the Hetzner
    ; bill. I also tried two uptime monitoring services, Nodeping and
    ; UptimeRobot.

2023-03-31 March 2023  ; commentary:
    ; First full month hosting mineshspc.com on Nevarro infrastructure. One
    ; node runs the website and a monitoring node runs Grafana + Loki. Adding
    ; more resources to the cluster won't need more monitoring nodes, so that
    ; cost should stay stable.

2023-03-31 Q1 2023  ; commentary:
    ; Nevarro LLC was formed on 24 January 2023 and incurred many startup
    ; costs in its first quarter, funded by an initial $1,500.00 capital
    ; contribution.
    ;
    ; Runway. $387.00 of this quarter's expenses were annual subscriptions.
    ; Amortized, that's $32.25/mo, plus $24.80/mo of other expenses, for an
    ; amortized burn of about $57/mo and roughly 18 months of runway.
    ;
    ; Looking ahead to Q2, the nevarro.space Matrix homeserver will move from
    ; Sumner's personal infrastructure (€25.75/mo) to Nevarro, raising Hetzner
    ; from €9.10/mo to about €34.85/mo. A few domain renewals are also due.

2023-04-30 April 2023  ; commentary:
    ; Two domain renewals came in, and I started migrating my Matrix server to
    ; Nevarro infrastructure.

2023-05-31 May 2023  ; commentary:
    ; The Twilio Sendgrid upgrade continued while HSPC email volume stayed
    ; high. I've since cancelled it, so we're back on the 100/month plan until
    ; registrations pick up again.
    ;
    ; I moved house, so the business address changed, which meant fees to the
    ; Colorado Secretary of State and USPS.

2023-06-30 Q2 2023  ; commentary:
    ; A quiet quarter; the main costs were maintaining servers. Burn was about
    ; $66/mo. Using a more conservative $75/mo gives roughly 12 months of
    ; runway. Server costs should stay at June levels next quarter.

2023-09-30 Q3 2023  ; commentary:
    ; Another quiet quarter of mostly server costs. Burn looks like $54/mo,
    ; but that's understated by the mid-quarter accounting change (Hetzner
    ; charges are now dated by the month they post). A better estimate is
    ; about $100/mo, or roughly 7 months of runway. Server costs should stay
    ; at September levels.

2023-12-31 December 2023  ; commentary:
    ; Nothing of note this month. I'll put another $1k into the company in
    ; January.

2023-12-31 Q4 2023  ; commentary:
    ; Mostly quiet, until a flurry of yearly subscriptions came due at the end
    ; of December. Burn was about $107/mo, roughly 2 months of runway, and
    ; even that is generous since several annual renewals land early in the
    ; year. Nevarro will need another cash infusion in January to stay
    ; solvent.
    ;
    ; Looking ahead to Q1 2024, server costs should stay at December levels.
    ; Several domain renewals and transfers are coming as I centralize all
    ; registrations in Namecheap (about $20/yr each).
